  ### Reason for requesting the library
  
  Druid looks up a number of its own classes and resources by name at runtime, and the jar ships no native-image metadata. In a native image nothing throws and the pool still hands out connections, but logging, filters and part of the JMX view stop working:
  
  - `LogFactory` probes for a logging backend with `Resources.classForName` and takes the `(String)` constructor of `SLF4JImpl`, `Log4jImpl`, `Log4j2Impl` and so on. None of them are registered, so it falls through to `NoLoggingImpl`, which only prints errors to stderr.
  - `FilterManager` reads the filter aliases from `META-INF/druid-filter.properties` and creates filters with `Class.newInstance()`. The resource is not in the image, so `filters=stat` is taken as a class name and the filter is dropped. No SQL stats are collected.
  - `DruidDataSourceStatManager` registers itself as a standard MBean, but `DruidDataSourceStatManagerMBean` is not registered for reflection, so the `DruidDataSourceStat` MBean has no attributes.
  
